#!/usr/bin/env bash

lord --verbose << "EOF"
Use the data from https://tanach.us/Tanach.html to properly attribute sources to the verses in [01][0-9]-*/*.tex.

Read master.tex and [01][0-9]-*/*.tex to see how we're currently assigning sources.

Then use the data for each verse, e.g., the XML that's available in the URLs with format https://tanach.us/Server.xml?Gen2:4-2:5
to assign sources correctly, especially focusing on getting the split location right in verses that are attributed to multiple
sources with a break in the middle.

Refer to MULTI-SOURCE-VERSES for a non-exhaustive list of what those verses are, but trust tanach.us over that file.

However, if you see any verses in which I've clearly done something manual to modify the Hebrew, leave that alone and don't remove it.

I just want the SPLIT LOCATIONS and SOURCE ATTRIBUTIONS to be updated via both \h?{...} and \e?{...}, I don't want you to edit or remove
any intra-verse word highlighting I might have done.

Do that now.
EOF
